---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/site/DocumentLayout.astro';
import Contact from '../components/site/Contact.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site/config';
export const prerender = true;
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="A clear view of what SalahSide stores, what Apple handles, and what you control."
  legal
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {
      site.publisher
        ? `${site.publisher} provides SalahSide.`
        : 'The SalahSide publisher will be identified before publication.'
    }
  </p>
  <p>
    {
      site.supportEmail ? (
        <>
          For privacy questions, contact <Contact subject="SalahSide privacy request" />.
        </>
      ) : (
        'Our support email will be added before launch.'
      )
    }
  </p>
  <h2>Your information stays close</h2>
  <p>
    The iPhone app does not require an account and has no application backend, advertising SDK,
    behavioral analytics SDK, or app cloud-sync service. It calculates prayer times from bundled
    coordinates for the city you select; it does not request GPS permission or send your city to us.
  </p>
  <p>
    On your device, SalahSide saves your city, calculation method, prayer conventions and minute
    adjustments, notification preferences, focus switches, self-reported prayer actions, temporary
    focus pause, and opaque Apple Screen Time selection tokens. Prayer history is limited to 90
    event records. Check-ins are voluntary and self-reported; the app does not verify worship.
  </p>
  <h2>Optional prayer mat unlock</h2>
  <p>
    If you register your own prayer mat, SalahSide uses the camera to take fresh photos and compares
    them on your iPhone. The app saves only a comparison fingerprint, a registration identifier, and
    the enabled setting in protected app-private storage. It does not save the captured photographs,
    add them to your photo library, or upload photographs or fingerprints. Captures stay in memory
    during review and processing and are discarded when you leave the capture flow.
  </p>
  <p>
    The fingerprint is not shared with widgets or Screen Time extensions. You can disable, replace,
    or remove the registered mat in Settings. Photo unlock is optional and does not verify prayer or
    establish that a photo contains a physical mat. Manual unlock remains available. Camera
    permission is requested only when you choose to take a photo.
  </p>
  <p>
    The mat profile is marked as excluded from backups. This is guidance to iOS, not a guarantee
    that it can never appear in a backup or restored device.
  </p>
  <h2>On-device extensions</h2>
  <p>
    Apple Screen Time extensions use a shared on-device App Group containing the minimum
    configuration, calculated schedule, release and pause state, and selection tokens needed for
    focus. The app and widgets also share a recognized subscription product identifier, verification
    time, and expiration time so membership features can stop when saved access expires.
  </p>
  <p>
    These extensions run on your device. SalahSide does not upload selected app identities,
    app-usage reports, or prayer history.
  </p>
  <h2>Apple purchases and services</h2>
  <p>
    Apple handles purchases, renewals, cancellation, and restoration through StoreKit. SalahSide
    receives verified subscription information to decide access. We do not receive your payment-card
    details. Apple's own services, diagnostic settings, and Apple account are governed by <a
      href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a
    >.
  </p>
  <h2>Optional permissions</h2>
  <p>
    Screen Time access, notifications, and camera permission are optional. Without Screen Time
    permission, prayer times and check-ins remain available with active membership. You can adjust
    focus switches, unlock a prayer, pause focus, and change permissions in iOS Settings.
    Notifications require permission and may be affected by your device's notification and Focus
    settings.
  </p>
  <h2>Storage, backup, and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Local data may be included in iOS device or iCloud backups according to your Apple backup
    settings. SalahSide does not promise exclusion from every backup.
  </p>
  <p>
    In SalahSide, open Settings and choose Erase local data to remove prayer settings, app
    selection, check-in history, and your registered mat and clear app-owned focus restrictions.
    This does not cancel an Apple subscription or remove existing device backups. Manage
    subscriptions and backups through Apple's settings.
  </p>
  <h2>This website and support email</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses no advertising trackers, analytics scripts, account system, or contact form.
    Its fonts and images are served with the site. The hosting service may process routine
    connection information, such as your IP address, requested page, and browser information, to
    deliver and secure the website under its retention settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you email support, we receive your email address, message, and any attachments you choose to
    send. We use them to answer your request and resolve the issue, retaining correspondence only as
    needed for that purpose or applicable obligations. Avoid sending sensitive information; prayer
    history and Screen Time selections are not needed for most requests. Email is handled by the
    selected email provider.
  </p>
  <h2>Requests and changes</h2>
  <p>
    {
      site.supportEmail ? (
        <>
          You can contact <Contact subject="SalahSide privacy request" /> about support
          correspondence or privacy questions.
        </>
      ) : (
        'Our support email will be added before launch for support correspondence and privacy questions.'
      )
    }
    We cannot remotely access or erase data stored only on your device. Depending on the law applicable
    to you, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal information you provide to us.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will update this page and its effective date when our data practices change. Questions about
    membership are covered in the <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> and <a href="/support/">Support</a> pages.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
